        <body>
            <div xml:id="d397">

                <pb facs="0745" n="621" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg621"/>

                <head>No. 393.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Evarts to Mr. Comly</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-03-02"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 2,
                        1881</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 90.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch No. 147, of the 17th of January last, reporting the proposed tour
                    around the world of King Kalakaua of Hawaii, accompaied by Attorney-General
                    Armstrong, and his chamberlain, Colonel Judd.</p>
                <p>It is confidently hoped that the tour of His Majesty may be fraught with many and
                    pleasant reminiscences during his extended journey, and that he may in the
                    course of his travels imbibe ideas, from his contact with foreign intercourse
                    and customs, which may be of practical utility to him for the future and
                    enlightened administration of his own government.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>WM. M. EVARTS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
